Report the RISC OS error when the game stops on one.

UnixLib turns a RISC OS error (SIGOSERROR) and a processor exception such
as a data abort (SIGEMT, "EMT trap") into a signal. Its report names the
signal and prints a backtrace, but for SIGEMT it leaves out the error
itself, which says what happened and where: "abort on data transfer at
&...", for example, shows whether the fault was in the game or in a module.
- On RISC OS, crashlog_unix.cpp catches SIGEMT and SIGOSERROR, prints
  "RISC OS error &<number>: <message>", then UnixLib's usual report.
- It ends with _exit, so a still-running thread no longer adds
  "terminate called without an active exception" to the log.

For OpenTTD 14.1. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-openttd.

diff --git a/src/os/unix/crashlog_unix.cpp b/src/os/unix/crashlog_unix.cpp
index 7ab97a7..656a734 100644
--- a/src/os/unix/crashlog_unix.cpp
+++ b/src/os/unix/crashlog_unix.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,11 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #endif
 
+#if defined(__riscos__)
+#	include <kernel.h>
+#	include <unixlib/local.h>
+#endif
+
 #include "../../safeguards.h"
 
 /** The signals we want our crash handler to handle. */
@@ -214,9 +219,33 @@ static void CDECL HandleCrash(int signum)
 	_exit(2);
 }
 
+#if defined(__riscos__)
+/**
+ * RISC OS: UnixLib turns a RISC OS error (SIGOSERROR) and a processor
+ * exception such as a data abort (SIGEMT) into a signal. Its own report names
+ * the signal and gives a backtrace, but leaves out the error itself, which
+ * says what went wrong and where (for example "Internal error: abort on data
+ * transfer at &..."). Print the error first, then UnixLib's usual report.
+ * @param signum The signal.
+ */
+static void CDECL HandleRiscOsError(int signum)
+{
+	const _kernel_oserror *e = _kernel_last_oserror();
+	if (e != nullptr) fmt::print(stderr, "\nRISC OS error &{:X}: {}\n", static_cast<uint32_t>(e->errnum), e->errmess);
+	__write_backtrace(signum);
+	/* _exit, not exit: static destructors (a joinable std::thread, say) would
+	 * only add "terminate called" to the report. */
+	_exit(2);
+}
+#endif
+
 /* static */ void CrashLog::InitialiseCrashLog()
 {
 	SetSignals(HandleCrash);
+#if defined(__riscos__)
+	signal(SIGEMT, HandleRiscOsError);
+	signal(SIGOSERROR, HandleRiscOsError);
+#endif
 }
 
 /* static */ void CrashLog::InitThread()
